        <item>
            <title>0.8</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:25:10 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>620</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.8</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.8 (build 620)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Tear panels off from their whole title bar.</b> The Playlist and Review Grade popups now have a title band across their top, like a Finder window, and dragging anywhere on it tears the panel off into a floating window.</li>
<li><b>Sessions find moved media on their own.</b> When a session&#8217;s media isn&#8217;t where the file says, Asobi searches the folders you have pointed it at before and the session&#8217;s own folders by name, and only asks for what is still missing.</li>
<li><b>Past Reviews.</b> The Shared Review panel keeps a list of every review link this Mac has shared: copy the link, see when it ran and what it held, and reopen the session it belonged to. Notes and marks live in the session, not the link; a link works while its review runs, up to seven days.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
